      "dom_id": "question-1780",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Suppose you have $5$ shirts, $4$ pants, and $9$ ties. How many outfits can be made consisting of a shirt, pants, and a tie?",
      "worked_solution": "Using the **rule of product**, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Number of outfits} & =\\text{Number of shirts} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of pants} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of ties} \\\\  & =5\\times 4\\times 9 \\\\  & =180.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $180$ different outfits can be made consisting of a shirt, pants, and a tie.",
