    {
      "dom_id": "question-1805",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "A word consists of $4$ letters, as shown below:\n\n| Letter | Letter | Letter | Letter |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n\nHere, each \"Letter\" can be any capital from A-Z ($26$ in total). How many possible words are there?",
      "worked_solution": "For each letter, there is a total of $26$ possibilities.\n\nUsing the **rule of product**, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Number of words} & =\\text{Number of options in the first slot} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of options in the second slot} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of options in the third slot} \\\\  & \\times \\text{Number of options in the fourth slot} \\\\  & =26\\times 26\\times 26\\times 26 \\\\  & ={26}^{4} \\\\  & =456\\,976.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, there are $456\\,976$ possible words.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
